    {
      "id": "F08",
      "category": "definition",
      "statement": "Contango means futures trade above spot, while Normal Backwardation describes futures trading below expected future spot due to convenience yield or hedger risk transfer. Embedded delivery options for timing, location, and cheapest-to-deliver grade favor the short seller and slightly depress futures prices.",
      "citation": {
        "chapter": "5",
        "section": "5.13",
        "page": "126"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "F09",
      "category": "numerical_example",
      "statement": "With spot S0 = 1.5000 dollars per pound, US rate r = 5.0% (0.05), UK rate rf = 8.0% (0.08), and T = 1 year, the spread is -0.03 (3% difference) and Covered Interest Parity gives F0 = 1.5000 * exp((0.05 - 0.08) * 1) = 1.4557 dollars per pound (forward discount).",
      "citation": {
        "chapter": "5",
        "section": "5.7",
        "page": "117"
      },
      "numbers": {
        "inputs": [
          {
            "symbol": "S0",
            "label": "Spot exchange rate",
            "value": 1.5,
            "unit": "dollars/GBP"
          },
          {
            "symbol": "r",
            "label": "US risk-free rate",
            "value": 0.05,
            "unit": "per year"
          },
          {
            "symbol": "rf",
            "label": "UK risk-free rate",
            "value": 0.08,
            "unit": "per year"
          },
          {
            "symbol": "T",
            "label": "Maturity horizon",
            "value": 1,
            "unit": "years"
          }
        ],
        "steps": [
          {
            "label": "Interest rate spread (3% difference)",
            "expr": "0.05 - 0.08",
            "value": -0.03
          },
          {
            "label": "Forward parity exchange rate",
            "expr": "1.5 * exp((0.05 - 0.08) * 1)",
            "value": 1.4557
          }
        ],
        "result": {
          "symbol": "F0",
          "label": "1-Year Forward Exchange Rate",
          "value": 1.4557,
          "unit": "dollars/GBP"
        },
        "rounding": 4
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "F10",
      "category": "numerical_example",
      "statement": "With euro spot S0 = 1.2500 dollars per euro, US rate r = 6.0% (0.06), and Eurozone rate rf = 4.0% (0.04) over T = 1 year, F0 = 1.2500 * exp((0.06 - 0.04) * 1) = 1.2753 dollars per euro (a forward premium because r exceeds rf; reversing the spread would falsely suggest 1.2252 and linear summing would give 1.3100).",
      "citation": {
